// // ============================================================================
// //  VM.KN — ISOLATED PROCESS EXECUTION WRAPPER
// //
// //  Invoked via the --vm CLI flag. Runs Kain tests inside an isolated
// //  subprocess, capturing stdout, stderr, and exit code for deterministic
// //  inspection — even for black-box / Heisenbug errors.
// //
// //  HOW IT WORKS:
// //    1. Locates the debug-template binary on disk
// //    2. Spawns it as a child process with the same test name but without --vm
// //    3. Captures stdout + stderr
// //    4. Waits for exit and reports results
// //
// //  ADVANCED: For deeper isolation, import markscript's bytecode VM.
// //    The markscript VM (X:\blades\markscript\src\vm.kn) provides a stack-based
// //    bytecode executor with full IVT dispatch, typed arithmetic, and handler
// //    chaining. To use it:
// //      1. Copy markscript/src/vm.kn, types.kn, error.kn into this template
// //      2. Compile your test logic to Markscript bytecode
// //      3. Execute through execute_bytecode() for complete determinism
// // ============================================================================
//
